{"id": "EUVD-2026-81735", "enisaUuid": "69bcac06-94df-31f4-9705-064d5928ab75", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvirtio_net: Fix resize of the RX ring\n\nWhen a AF_XDP socket is attached, the virtnet_rx_resize\nshould resize the rq->xsk_buffs XSK buffer array. Otherwise,\nwhen the size grows, the virtnet_rx_resume() causes a write\npast the end of the array. This is easily reproducable with\n\n    ethtool -G ens3 rx 32\n    ./xdpsock -i eth0 -q 0 -r -z &\n    ethtool -G eth0 rx 256", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:02", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c941b5d989a15cdaa987a2c602fb168461c6186", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5235abdb760bbd7a6fcecf1890b5160b7a75a9ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8344c9233c8f77017174d9e280c5a26034d068b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d09c98a6da215bce2173a292e4b95c8de6ea5d51"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2rwj-7pmr-4q35", "CVE-2026-90142"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0162923f-2a00-3d16-97b4-e640c03d6f86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "44afa7aa-8a06-3597-8b22-e0a7317b40f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e9f3962441c0a4d6f16c656e6c8aa02a3ccdd568 <8344c9233c8f77017174d9e280c5a26034d068b6"}, {"id": "515d6473-6efd-3810-8ac1-9ac9490c8a3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "5ab746a3-1945-3445-92db-db3f18717006", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "7c9763d3-2455-3838-bae0-cb451fd44877", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e9f3962441c0a4d6f16c656e6c8aa02a3ccdd568 <5c941b5d989a15cdaa987a2c602fb168461c6186